From 9bcfd27e636e57299355cd7bdeec465149276318 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:34:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Custom missions are playable: authored-mission delivery +
 practice sandbox
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the gap where teacher-authored missions/scenarios could be created but
never played. Students play them from Classroom -> My dashboard -> Play custom
missions.

- supabase/m10-authored-delivery.sql: get_class_missions() SECURITY DEFINER
  returns exactly the authored missions assigned to a class (directly or via a
  scenario) to its members, nothing to outsiders. + m10-delivery-test.sql
  (6 assertions) wired into run.sh.
- Check engine (authoredCheck): maps the 5 editor check types (file_exists,
  file_contains, file_matches, command_run, service_state) to live checks.
- Practice sandbox (playAuthored/practiceFinish/exitPractice): runs authored
  missions in a throwaway state like Race — campaign progress untouched;
  completing one records an attempts row by mission id so the grade updates.
  Single mission auto-finishes; sequences get an Exit practice button.
- Student dashboard: a "Play custom missions" button per class, fed by
  get_class_missions.
- Editor copy updated (safe check types / no file pre-seeding).
- test-authored-playback.js (npm run test:play): end-to-end — launches a
  delivered mission, solves it, asserts the attempt is recorded.
- Cache v24 -> v25.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q9A1atnfLsQUP5DWZ8rYYW
